The probability of no snow on any given day is $1-\frac{3}{4}=\frac{1}{4}$.
Since the probabilities are independent, the probability of no snow on all three days is $\left(\frac{1}{4}\right)^3=\frac{1}{4^3}=\frac{1}{64}$.
Therefore, the probability that there will be no snow at all during the next three days is $\boxed{\frac{1}{64}}$.The answer is: \frac{1}{64}

