We can write
\[\left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| = \frac{|\beta - \alpha|}{|1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta|}.\]Since $|\beta| = 1,$ $|\beta - \alpha|$ is the distance between $\alpha$ and $\beta$ in the complex plane.  Let $P$ and $Q$ be the points corresponding to $\alpha$ and $\beta,$ respectively.  Then $|PQ| = |\beta - \alpha|$:

[asy]
