Thus, we want to maximize
\[\frac{|\beta - \alpha|}{|1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta|} = \frac{|PQ|}{|1 - \overline{P} Q|}.\]By the Triangle Inequality,
\[|PQ + 1 - \overline{P} Q| \ge |PQ| - |1 - \overline{P} Q|.\]Then
\[|1 - \overline{P} Q| \le |PQ| - |PQ + 1 - \overline{P} Q| = 1,\]so
\[\frac{|PQ|}{|1 - \overline{P} Q|} \le |PQ|.\]Equality occurs when $Q = -1,$ so the maximum value is $\boxed{1}.$

