Let $c$ be the number of pounds of corn and $b$ be the number of pounds of beans.
We can set up a system of equations to represent the given information:
\begin{align*}
c + b &= 24 \\
0.99c + 0.45b &= 18.09
\end{align*}
To eliminate decimals, we can multiply the second equation by 100 to get:
\begin{align*}
99c + 45b &= 1809
\end{align*}
We can then multiply the first equation by 45 to get:
\begin{align*}
45c + 45b &= 1080
\end{align*}
We can subtract the second equation from the first equation to eliminate $b$:
\begin{align*}
(45c + 45b) - (99c + 45b) &= 1080 - 1809 \\
-54c &= -729 \\
c &= \frac{729}{54} \\
c &\approx 13.5
\end{align*}
